The Bally Basic (All gold label) uses the 300 baud interface. That is a separate unit that you will need to buy. Then you need standard 3.5 mm cables with plugs on both ends so that you can plug them into the interface and a portable tape player. big home cassette players will work, but they are hard to adjust the volume and tone controls correctly.  This is the interface that plugs into the  light pen and a joystick port to work. This will NOT input a 2000 baud saved program, nor can it save at 2000 baud.

The Astrobasic cartridge  has it's own interface built into the cartridge. It  nly works  at 2000 baud.
All it needs is one of the 3.5mm cables and you switch it back and forth between the earphone and microphone jacks on your cassette recorder depending on whether you are bringing in a prerecorded progrwm or you are saving a program to the cassette tape. This does NOT need to plug into any other place on the Astrocade. This will not work with 300 baud programs.

I hope this answers your question.
Ken














