            I have added a new audio section to Ballyalley.com to hold miscellaneous 

Astrocade audio (non-progam) files.  Currently only two files are there 

(WaveMakers intros).  This section is a great place to hold any audio that 

is Astrocade related.  A few years ago Lance F. Squire recorded a couple of 

songs by George Moses.  This new area is a perfect place for material like 

that!



If you record any music out of the Astrocade and would like to have it added 

to this area, then upload it to the Bally Alley discussion group and I'll 

see that it is added to the web site.



If you're wondering HOW to record music (or game sounds) from your 

Astrocade; here is a rather straight-forward approach:



1) Plug your Astrocade into the TV as normal.



2) Take a cable from your TV's audio out (for headphones)- - if your TV has 

one-- and plug it into the audio-in of your computer's sound card.  If your 

TV doesn't have a headphone jack, then I'm not sure how to do it.  Anyone 

have any idea?


Most modern TVs have "audio out" jacks (RCA red and white, yellow is video) Use a cable that has an RCA jack on one side and a 3.5mm plug on the other side. Plug the 3.5mm plug into the computer's audio in jack. Then do step 3


3) Record the music, or sounds using your favorite audio recording software. 

  I personally use an eleven year old shareware program called "Cool Edit 

96," but even Windows Media Player should work fine.



Try recording something and ABOVE ALL...



Have FUN!



Adam



